<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<head>
    <%- include('../partials/header.ejs') %>
        <title>GTIA | Academic Resources</title>
        <link href="../../assets/sun/css/style.css" rel="stylesheet" />
        <link href="../../assets/sun/css/resources.css" rel="stylesheet" />
</head>

<body>
    <%- include('../partials/navbar.ejs', { currentPage: 'academics' }) %>

        <div class="container py-5" id="academics">
            <h1 class="text-center">Academic Resources</h1>

            <section class="pt-1">
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="pl-5">
                        <h3 class="color-dark-primary">What are some useful general academic resources for
                            Tech
                            students?</h3>
                        <p class="color-dark-secondary pt-3">
                            Course scheduling and registration at Georgia Tech is a process that spans 1-2
                            months.
                            Any student may plan a four year schedule by looking at the <a class="color-primary"
                                href="http://catalog.gatech.edu" target="_blank">Course Catalog</a>. This lists
                            all
                            the requirements that students must fulfill in addition to their major
                            requirements
                            to
                            complete the degree. Students can reach out to their Academic Advisors for
                            assistance in
                            planning their course load for the following semester.
                        </p>
                        <p class="color-dark-secondary ">
                            The following are tools that students utilize for course planning:
                        </p>
                        <ul class="color-dark-secondary ">
                            <li><a class="color-primary" href="https://www.gt-scheduler.org" target="_blank">GT
                                    Scheduler</a>: This a recently-developed (by Tech students!) website
                                that
                                ties
                                together all the tools mentioned below! </li>
                            <li><a class="color-primary" href="https://gatech.courseoff.com"
                                    target="_blank">Courseoff</a>: A website for students to plan their
                                schedules
                                ahead of registration and simplifies the registration process. Besides
                                offering
                                a
                                color coded scheme for various classes, it enables students to select any
                                particular
                                class offered in the current/future semester, view the timings and class
                                capacity,
                                professors teaching those classes, and the course CRNs. CRN numbers are
                                uniquely
                                assigned to each class which can later be inputted during registration to
                                quickly
                                get the desired classes.</li>
                            <li><a class="color-primary"
                                    href="https://www.ratemyprofessors.com/campusRatings.jsp?sid=361"
                                    target="_blank">RateMyProfessor</a>: A website that allows students to
                                view
                                reviews and ratings of professors for multiple subjects based on student
                                feedback.
                            </li>
                            <li><a class="color-primary" href="https://critique.gatech.edu/" target="_blank">Course
                                    Critique</a> and <a class="color-primary"
                                    href="https://lite.gatech.edu/lite_script/dashboards/grade_distribution.html"
                                    target="_blank">Georgia Tech's Grade Distribution Dashboard</a>: These
                                websites
                                provide students information on the grade distribution (GPA) for different
                                courses
                                and professors over a span of 5-10 years.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="color-dark-secondary ">
                            Georgia Tech students reference these tools to gauge a preliminary understanding
                            of
                            the
                            course and how it might go, but it isn’t representative of everything the
                            classes
                            and
                            professors entail.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="pt-5">
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="pl-5">
                        <h3 class="color-dark-primary">What study abroad opportunities are available at
                            Tech?
                        </h3>
                        <p class="color-dark-secondary pt-3">
                            Each year, more than 1,500 Tech students study at over 120 study abroad
                            programs.
                            Two
                            kinds of study abroad programs are offered: GT Faculty-Led and Exchange (not
                            GT-affiliated), and they can be either general or major-specific. Popular
                            programs
                            include Georgia Tech Lorraine, Oxford Summer Program, EU Brussels Summer
                            Program,
                            and
                            the Pacific Program. You can use the <a href="https://oie.gatech.edu/study-abroad-programs"
                                class="color-primary" target="_blank">Study Abroad Program Finder</a> to assist you in
                            your
                            international
                            education experience search.
                        </p>
                        <p class="color-dark-secondary ">
                            Additionally, students can pursue the International Plan (IP), which includes 26
                            weeks
                            of international experience (work, research, of study). IP's goal is to promote
                            a
                            deeper
                            understanding of the global environment and to develop proficiency in a language
                            other
                            than English.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="pt-5">
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="pl-5">
                        <h3 class="color-dark-primary">What academic support and advising resources are
                            available at
                            Tech?</h3>
                        <p class="color-dark-secondary pt-3">
                            There are numerous tutoring resources available on campus, which aid a student
                            to
                            succeed in his/her coursework. The <a class="color-primary"
                                href="https://tutoring.gatech.edu/" target="_blank">Tutoring & Academic
                                Support
                                Center</a> located in the Clough Undergraduate Learning Commons (CULC)
                            offers
                            many
                            such opportunities. Below are additional resources to take advantage of as a
                            student:
                        </p>
                        <ul class="color-dark-secondary ">
                            <li><a class="color-primary" href="http://www.omed.gatech.edu/" target="_blank">OMED</a>:
                                The Office of Minority Educational Development
                                offers
                                study sessions for classes that are er and topic-specific.</li>
                            <li><a class="color-primary" href="https://www.communicationcenter.gatech.edu/"
                                    target="_blank">Communication Center</a>: The Communication Lab provides
                                assistance to students on assignments or projects relating to communication,
                                as
                                well
                                as on cover letters, resumes, interview preparation etc.</li>
                            <li>Office Hours: All professors hold office hours, which are specific times set
                                by
                                the
                                professor outside of regular class time that students can use to clarify
                                doubts,
                                ask
                                questions, etc. For some subjects, the Teacher Assistants (TAs) also hold
                                their
                                own
                                office hours. The schedule of Office Hours is given by the professor or the
                                TA
                                on
                                the first/second day of class and can usually be found on the class
                                syllabus.
                            </li>
                            <li><a class="color-primary" href="https://advising.gatech.edu/students"
                                    target="_blank">Advising</a>: Every student is assigned a major advisor
                                who
                                offers advising related to class class registration, internships/co-ops, and
                                undergraduate research. In addition, students are also assigned individual
                                academic
                                advisors whom they can consult on a regular basis. Students are encouraged
                                to
                                meet
                                with their advisor at least twice per semester.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>
        </div>

        <%- include('../partials/footer.ejs') %>
</body>

</html>